.TH PLZ-RUN 1 "August 2026" "plz-run" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
plz-run \- run a program through the systemd system manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B plz-run
.RI [ options ]
.I program
.RI [ arguments ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B plz-run
asks systemd to start a transient service for the requested program. Standard
input, standard output, and standard error are passed to the service, and the
program's exit status is returned to the caller.
.PP
The caller needs permission to access the system bus and to ask systemd to
start the transient service. This can be used to run a program across a
sandbox boundary when the confinement policy grants those permissions.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-u " user"
Run the program as the specified user.
.TP
.BI \-g " group"
Run the program as the specified group.
.TP
.BI \-E " name=value"
Add an environment variable. This option may be specified more than once.
.TP
.BI \-pam " name"
Set the systemd PAMName property.
.TP
.BI \-C " directory"
Set the working directory.
.TP
.B \-same-dir
Use the caller's current working directory. This cannot be combined with
.BR \-C .
.TP
.BI \-log-level " level"
Set the internal logging level.
.TP
.B \-expand-var
Allow systemd to expand variables in program arguments. By default, dollar
signs are escaped before the request is sent to systemd.
.TP
.BI \-ambient-capabilities " bitset"
Set the systemd AmbientCapabilities property to the given decimal bitset.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The payload's exit status is returned when it exits normally. An error is
reported if the transient service cannot be started or its result cannot be
interpreted.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemd-run (1),
.BR systemd.service (5)
